  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "985ec034",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Caveats\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this notebook can say**\n",
    "- How well Bond-ness is ranked under leave-one-actor-out CV, versus a\n",
    "  training-free cosine-to-Bond-centroid baseline.\n",
    "- Which PCA directions and embedding dimensions move the decision.\n",
    "- Whether adding `heightCm` changes the ranking at actor level.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What it cannot say**\n",
    "- **It is not a casting judgement.** The score is *resemblance to the six past\n",
    "  Bonds as photographed here*. Bond-fit is a commercial and cultural decision;\n",
    "  this measures face geometry.\n",
    "- **Six positives, one background.** All six positives are white male actors,\n",
    "  mostly English/Irish, filmed by the same franchise over 60 years. The model can\n",
    "  learn \"looks like this specific cohort\" and still be useless for any real\n",
    "  casting question. That confound is not fixable by more negatives.\n",
    "- **AUC and AP here are coarse.** With ~6 positives, each positive moves AP by a\n",
    "  visible amount, and one hard negative can swing the number. Report the per-Bond\n",
    "  ranks next to any AUC, and do not quote a decimal place's difference as a finding.\n",
    "- **No separate test set.** `k` and `C` are chosen on the same group CV used to\n",
    "  report. That is a mild optimism; the honest reading is \"these settings work on\n",
    "  this data\", not \"generalises\".\n",
    "- **Negatives are not neutral.** Which non-Bond actors you choose *is* the\n",
    "  experiment. Add varied ages, ethnicities, and looks, or the model learns to\n",
    "  separate \"these six men\" from \"anyone the dataset author picked\".\n",
    "- **The demo is one data point.** A single held-out actor cannot validate or\n",
    "  invalidate the model; it is an illustration. Hold out several actors across\n",
    "  multiple runs to get a real read.\n",
    "- **Closed-set intuition does not transfer.** There is no \"none of the above\"\n",
    "  output — every face gets a Bond-likeness score, and that score is not\n",
    "  calibrated. Do not threshold it as a probability without calibration data.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Highest-value next steps**\n",
    "1. **More negatives, deliberately varied** — this is the whole experiment.\n",
    "2. **More positives per Bond** so the centroid and the per-Bond ranks are stable.\n",
    "3. **Hold out several actors, repeatedly**, and report the spread rather than a\n",
    "   single fold's number.\n",
    "4. **Calibrate** (`CalibratedClassifierCV`) before using `fit_probability` as\n",
    "   anything other than a ranking key."
   ]
  }
 ],
